# Line endings, and why this file exists.
#
# This is a template other people clone, and a fair number of them clone it on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true. Without this file the shell scripts and the
# Dockerfile check out CRLF, and `docker compose up --build` then copies a
# CRLF entrypoint into the image. Its shebang becomes `#!/bin/sh\r`, the
# container cannot exec it, the runtime placeholders are never replaced, and
# the app renders with the literal string __RT_VITE_INSTANCE_NAME__ as its
# title. Nothing in that chain says "line endings" to the person debugging it.
#
# Anything read by a Linux container or an interpreter is pinned to LF.
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never rewrites bytes inside them.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
